### 1. Executive Summary & Breach Closure

In the original kill table for `ppcrldimimask` ([PRETABLE.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/ppcrldimimask/killtable_20260911/PRETABLE.out#L69) and [SCORES.txt](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/ppcrldimimask/killtable_20260911/SCORES.txt#L49-L54)), vacuity-floor clause (c) was ostensibly discharged by:
```
(c) null medium -> HEAD leg (whole-file pre-fix)
```
scoring **17/27** (identical to `M_ORIG`, the verbatim defect reinstatement). 

Per owner ruling on 2026-09-11 (*"Null-medium sweep: AUDIT, THEN RE-RUN THE BREACHES"*), this represented an unswept clause (c) breach: a pre-fix build measures **clause (a)** (detector must fail on the pre-fix build), not **clause (c)** (detector must fail on a medium carrying *none* of the behaviour under test). That table had two legs measuring one thing and no null medium.

The honest null medium has been built, compiled, measured, and verified in scratch clone `/tmp/gxrldimi_clone` with the sentinel discipline strictly adhered to.

